            <ArticleTitle>Pharmacological and clinical importance of narcotic antagonists and mixed antagonists--use in cardiology.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>309S-311S</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>1 The treatment of pain of cardiac origin requires a knowledge of the haemodynamic action of the analgesic agents used. 2 The haemodynamic effects of morphine, diamorphine, pavaveretum, pethidine and pentazocine are reviewed. 3 Clinical experience with the new antagonist analgesic buprenorphine is reported. 4 These studies indicate that buprenorphine may be the agent of choice for the relief of severe pain in patients with unstable circulation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
